          "notes": "Four stations are seasonally monitored collecting phyto- and zoobenthos samples, as well as the main environmental variables (temperature, salinity, ph, O2). Moreover temperature sensors are immersed for continuous measurements . Starting from winter 2016, an additional station was monitored, since the presence of an alien species of macroalga and the seagrass Cymodocea nodosa were here detected.",
          "siteVisitInterval": 90
        },
        "notes": "There are no built infrastructures in the Mar Piccolo, neither permanent measurements equipments (i.e. buoys) only mobile equipments brought during sampling operations. Permanent little data logger are submersed for continuous temperature measurements",
